Title: main_sweep --after hides tips the after-merge runner never checked
Created: 2026-10-27
Author: reviewer

--- log ---
2026-10-27T19:30Z reviewer created

--- body ---
## Context
Found by 1283's Imagine pass (raid 2026-10-27b): after PR #1799, padme's after-merge runner crashed 10 times
(`AttributeError: module 'raid_land' has no attribute 'GhForge'`, `.git/idh/after-merge.log`) before writing any record,
so tips 01e2d72f and the 9 after it have no after-merge record. `scripts/main_sweep.py --after` lists only tips newer
than the newest record; the green record on dc0fc78e (#1811) therefore hid every unchecked tip before it. A runner
crash leaves no red ticket and no sweep finding: red tips can go unseen.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] main_sweep reports first-parent main tips since the last sweep that carry no after-merge record, even when a newer record exists.
- [ ] A test with a recordless tip older than a green record shows it listed.
- [ ] The harness gate passes.

Related: [[1283]], [[1265]].

## Feasibility (raid 2026-10-27b)
WARN: no plan yet; files scripts/main_sweep.py (after_gaps, ~:138) and tests/test_after_merge.py. The documented rule that a result covers every tip it passed over (merge-gate.py:59) must be reconciled: the coder first states how a crashed-on tip is told apart from a passed-over one (e.g. the runner logs or marks a start for each tip it attempts), then implements. Wave 3, after 1283.
